@base = http://127.0.0.1:18103
@key = local-paypal-key
@admin = local-admin-key

### Create an order; amount is a decimal string
POST {{base}}/v2/checkout/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
PayPal-Request-Id: paypal-lesson-001
X-Simulator-Payment-Method: pm_funded
Content-Type: application/json

{"intent":"CAPTURE","purchase_units":[{"custom_id":"paypal-lesson-001","amount":{"currency_code":"EUR","value":"25.00"}}]}

> {% client.global.set("paypalId", response.body.id); %}

### Try capture before approval: expect 409 and no financial effect
POST {{base}}/v2/checkout/orders/{{paypalId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
PayPal-Request-Id: paypal-capture-001
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### LOCAL substitute for buyer approval (not a real PayPal endpoint)
POST {{base}}/__sim/orders/{{paypalId}}/approve
X-Simulator-Admin-Key: {{admin}}
PayPal-Request-Id: paypal-approve-001
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Now repeat the capture; expect COMPLETED
POST {{base}}/v2/checkout/orders/{{paypalId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}
PayPal-Request-Id: paypal-capture-001
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Observe the current order
GET {{base}}/v2/checkout/orders/{{paypalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{key}}

### Check the financial evidence
GET {{base}}/__sim/payments/{{paypalId}}/ledger
X-Simulator-Admin-Key: {{admin}}
